From 3ae27a7a9e8314fd18f53d2cbc3db948260dc64c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kayori <thatzokay@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:29:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 28/30] grate: blend with any factor pair and equation, and
 honour the colormask

The 3D unit has no blender: a blended program is the application's program
plus one more sequencer instruction that reads the destination pixel into
R0/R1 and a few ALU packets that combine it with the colour in R2/R3. The
only epilogue was the premultiplied source-over one, built once per
program; any other blend state was logged and drawn unblended.

The epilogue is now generated from the blend state (fp/blend.c) and built
on first use, one variant per state and program (struct grate_blend_variant):

* equations ADD, SUBTRACT, REVERSE_SUBTRACT, separate for rgb and alpha;
* factors ZERO, ONE, (INV_)SRC_COLOR, (INV_)SRC_ALPHA, (INV_)DST_COLOR,
  (INV_)DST_ALPHA, separate for rgb and alpha;
* the colormask, also with blending off.

One ALU slot computes A * B + C, and C * D only when D is a half of the
register C is in, so per position (B, G, R, A) either "dst * Fd + src"
(source factor ONE or ZERO, one packet, the old epilogue) or
"G = src * Fs" into a global, a nop packet, then "dst * Fd +/- G".

Factors and equations are rows in tables (blend_factors[], blend_funcs[]);
anything not in them makes grate_fp_blend_key() return 0 and the bind logs
the whole state. See the comment at the top of blend.c for how to extend it.
Not supported yet: constant colour factors, SRC_ALPHA_SATURATE, MIN/MAX,
logic ops.
